{"id": "EUVD-2026-63991", "enisaUuid": "566e82cc-e0ff-3435-8ee2-8a39327fbef6", "description": "Paperclip before 0.3.1 in default local_trusted mode fails to validate Host headers, allowing attackers to execute arbitrary commands via DNS rebinding. An attacker can craft a malicious webpage that, when visited by a developer running Paperclip locally, uses DNS rebinding to make authenticated API requests and execute commands through the process adapter.", "datePublished": "2026-08-21T15:03:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-01T19:19:28", "baseScore": 9.4, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H", "references": ["https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/security/advisories/GHSA-x8hx-rhr2-9rf7", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/paperclip-before-remote-code-execution-via-dns-rebinding"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-77087", "GHSA-gwmj-hf32-5v8v"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.49, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a14b1b94-1749-384c-bbbd-ed7a6b6755d3", "product": {"name": "paperclip", "vendor": {"name": "paperclipai"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.3.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3b0199f9-d2e5-386f-ba7f-79793baa0b55", "vendor": {"name": "paperclipai"}}], "isExploited": false}